<article class="env-definition" id="02PZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02PZ">Definition <span data-tag="02PZ">42.68.29</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian local ring with residue field $\kappa $. Let $a, b \in A$. Let $M$ be a finite $A$-module of dimension $1$ such that $a, b$ are nonzerodivisors on $M$. We define the <em>symbol associated to $M, a, b$</em> to be the element </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  d_ M(a, b) = \det \nolimits _\kappa (M/abM, a, b) \in \kappa ^*  \]
</div>
</article>